{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Prim’s algorithm reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra visitor, which its Prim uses."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PrimEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Weight"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree is started at a vertex not yet spanned. Then, while a vertex is waiting to join, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one with the lightest key is examined: it joins the tree through the edge that gave it that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key (none for the start). Each of its edges whose far end is not yet spanned is examined with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its weight, then relaxed, when the weight is below the far end’s key or the far end was not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yet waiting, or not relaxed. An edge whose far end is already spanned, a self-loop included,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is skipped without an event and without being weighed. After its last edge the examined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex is finished. Over every component, the next tree starts at the first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order that is not spanned."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/primevent"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/edgeRelaxed(_:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/examine(_:edge:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/examineEdge(_:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/finish(_:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/startVertex(_:)"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PrimEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kin